  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, due to its nature, location, excessive height and design, would result in a dominant and unsympathetic form of development, which would fail to respect the existing dwelling and would not integrate well within its context, appearing as an overly prominent addition to the front amenity area of the dwelling and resulting in a significant negative impact on the appearance of the existing property, the setting of the group of terraced houses with prevailing open frontages and the Courteney Avenue street scene. As such, the proposal is contrary to policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and the guidance as set out within SPD 4 'Design of Residential Extensions'.",
    "In the absence of a specialised BS 4142 noise assessment report to indicate otherwise, the proposed development would have an adverse impact on the amenities of the adjoining properties by way of increased noise and disturbance, contrary to Policy 29 of Sutton Local Plan 2018.\r"
